  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all confirmed incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 24 hours, with a confirmed-incident scope. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% threshold but exceeding it triggers corrective action rather than an automatic sales ban, with results to regulators and customers but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off from adoption and 6-year retrofit where feasible; S4 mandates built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 uses an 8-per-100k investigation trigger rather than automatic recall, with prompt customer notice."
